WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:06.440
The entertainment world lost one of its most
iconic performers on Sunday, January 9.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:12.099
TMZ reported that Bob Saget was found deceased
in his Ritz-Carlton hotel room in Orlando,

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:15.130
Florida at approximately 4 p.m. ET.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:19.810
The Orange County Sheriff's Office tweeted
out more details a few hours later, elaborating

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.599
that "detectives found no signs of foul play
or drug use in this case."

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:29.919
As of the making of this video, it is still
unclear what the exact cause of death is,

00:00:29.919 --> 00:00:32.950
and it may take time before that information
is made public.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:37.540
In a statement issued after the announcement
of Saget's passing, his family said,

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:42.580
"We are devastated to confirm that our beloved
Bob passed away today ... He was everything

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:47.420
to us and we want you to know how much he
loved his fans, performing live and bringing

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.970
people from all walks of life together with
laughter ... Though we ask for privacy at

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:56.880
this time, we invite you to join us in remembering
the love and laughter that Bob brought to

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:57.880
the world."

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:02.020
As seen on both his Twitter and Instagram
accounts, the actor and stand-up comedian

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:06.420
shared a photo from the stage of the venue
where he most recently performed — less

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.399
than 24 hours before his passing.

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:11.990
In his post, where he is seen smiling, he
wrote,

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.549
"I had no idea I did a two hour set tonight.

00:01:14.549 --> 00:01:17.320
I’m back in comedy like I was when I was
26.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.659
I guess I’m finding my new voice and loving
every moment of it."

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:24.679
Bob Saget led a very interesting career which
spanned more than 40 years.

00:01:24.679 --> 00:01:29.530
Of course, his most well-known role is playing
the widowed father of three, Danny Tanner,

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.630
on the popular late '80s and '90s sitcom "Full
House."

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:37.350
The show ran for eight years, and he later
reprised the same role when the "Fuller House"

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.600
reboot launched on Netflix in 2016.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.670
Saget's career in television was, of course,
more prolific than his role on the hit ABC

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:45.670
sitcom.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:50.700
The "Full House" alum also hosted the popular
series "America's Funniest Home Videos," beginning

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.729
in 1989 and ending in 1997.

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:59.009
On the heels of these two gigs, Saget returned
to television dad territory with The WB sitcom

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:02.600
"Raising Dad," co-starring Brie Larson and
Kat Dennings.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.549
Additionally, Saget can be heard as the Narrator
of the series "How I Met Your Mother," where

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:11.870
he takes on the role of the older version
of Ted Moseby, played in flashbacks on the

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.540
show by Josh Radnor.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.840
"Kids, I'm going to tell you an incredible
story.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.210
The story of how I met your mother."

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:24.320
In contrast to his more wholesome, family-friendly
television work, Saget was also well-known

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.680
for his delightfully vulgar and boundary-pushing
stand-up comedy.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.480
Audiences got a taste of this on-screen thanks
to Saget's voice role in 2006's "Farce of

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:39.220
the Penguins," and an appearance in the documentary
"The Aristocrats," a film about the most infamous

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.520
dirty joke in the standup comedy world.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.290
Despite his success on TV, taking to the stage
to perform standup appeared to be something

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.080
that never got old for Saget.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.520
"I am dirty.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.520
Apparently I am dirty."

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.260
If you've ever seen one of Bob Saget's taped
stand-up specials or had the pleasure of seeing

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:59.320
him perform live, then you likely know that
his stand-up comedy was often a departure

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.400
from the more family-oriented TV shows that
he became well-known for.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.500
Saget was still touring as a stand-up at the
time of his death and based on interviews

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.900
he gave in his final years, it sounds as though
he took great pleasure in being able to make

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.070
people laugh.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:17.990
In 2017, Saget spoke to The Tennessean in
the midst of a four-month standup tour.

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:18.990
He told the publication,

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:22.460
"It's like, 'How can I be 60 and still love
this so much?'"

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.930
It seems that love only grew stronger.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:30.530
When asked by Alabama.com about how the COVID-19
pandemic had affected his standup career,

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.690
Saget discussed pivoting to podcasts.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:37.850
However, he also shared that being away from
live audiences only made his heart grow fonder.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.850
The comedian revealed,

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:43.160
"But stand-up, once I was able to get back
to it, it really took me only one show to

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.100
really get into it and realize how much I
loved it.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.620
More than I have since, you know, 1995."

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:53.130
Saget's love of entertaining was clearly reflected
in the number of people who turned to his

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.420
humor for comfort.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:59.210
Whether you knew him best for his fatherly
persona on TV or his edgier standup, Saget

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.510
will be sorely missed.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:04.070
His contributions to the entertainment world
will be remembered for years to come.

